  <prompt>
    Two coupled fixes to the regarding target set:

    1. **Add `sprk_event`** to the regarding catalog + priority as the sixth association target: additive entries in `CommunicationService.RegardingLookupMap`, `IncomingAssociationResolver.RegardingFieldPriority`, and `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG` (mirror task 003's pattern for `sprk_servicerequest`). The `sprk_regardingevent` lookup should already exist or be confirmed on `sprk_communication` — verify via MCP; if absent, note it (do NOT create it here — flag for a schema follow-up if needed).

    2. **Correct the organization association target to `sprk_organization`** (DEC-3, requirement #15). The current sender-domain match writes an OOB `account` regarding — WRONG. Fix it so a domain match writes `sprk_regardingorganization` → `sprk_organization` (Spaarke's first-class org entity), NOT OOB `account` and NOT OOB `organization`. No code path may write `account` for org association after this task.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer authoritative on `Services/Communication/` — `IncomingAssociationResolver` sender-domain matching, `CommunicationService.RegardingLookupMap`, and the ADR-024 regarding-write path. Familiar with the binding `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` governance checklist.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `sprk_event` is a resolvable association target (map + priority + catalog wired). The sender-domain org match writes `sprk_regardingorganization` → `sprk_organization`; grep confirms no remaining code path writes an OOB `account` (or OOB `organization`) regarding for org association. Build clean; existing Communication tests pass (plus a new/updated test asserting the org target); publish-size + CVE reported; placement justification stated.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R4 extends the Association Engine to eight targets. `sprk_event` is the sixth (task 003 added `sprk_servicerequest`, the fourth). Separately, the existing inbound resolver has a latent correctness bug: its sender-domain match (org-by-domain) resolves to the OOB Dataverse `account` entity, but Spaarke's first-class organization entity is `sprk_organization`. DEC-3 / requirement #15 correct this. Because this is a behavioral change to the live inbound resolver (not merely additive), it is FULL rigor.

      The org-target correction here is the schema/wiring foundation; task 013 (W1 rung 2) builds the fuller org-by-domain participant-correlation logic on top of the corrected target.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingAssociationResolver.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">FR-04 / DEC-3 / req #15: domain match MUST write `sprk_regardingorganization` → `sprk_organization`. NO path may write OOB `account` or OOB `organization` for org association after this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Extend the existing regarding family — additive `sprk_event` entry across map/priority/catalog. Keep writing ADR-024 typed lookups + denormalized fields.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (§11)">MUST NOT add a new regarding mechanism. `sprk_event` is additive; the org fix is a target correction, not a new abstraction.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (§10 BFF Hygiene)">State the Placement Justification in the PR/design even though the change stays in BFF (`Services/Communication/`). Load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (NFR-02)">Report publish-size (absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs baseline). Expected ≈ 0 delta (no packages added).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Run `/conflict-check` before opening the PR (BFF-touching; `Services/Ai` sole-owned by `spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2` — this task touches `Services/Communication`, low overlap, but the check is mandatory).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Task 005 codifies the engine target contract; keep `sprk_event` + the org correction consistent with it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/spec.md</file>
