    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Regarding target extension" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs">
        `RegardingLookupMap` maps entity logical name → regarding lookup field. Add `sprk_event` → `sprk_regardingevent`. Mirror in `RegardingFieldPriority` + `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG` (same additive pattern task 003 used for `sprk_servicerequest`).
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Org target correction" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingAssociationResolver.cs">
        Locate the sender-domain match that resolves the org regarding. Replace the `account` target with `sprk_organization` + `sprk_regardingorganization`. Grep the whole `Services/Communication/` tree for any other `account` org-association write.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Read `IncomingAssociationResolver.cs` sender-domain match + `CommunicationService.RegardingLookupMap` + `RegardingFieldPriority` + `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`.</step>
    <step order="2">Grep `Services/Communication/` for `account` and `sprk_regardingorganization` — enumerate every org-association write site. Confirm which write the OOB `account` target.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify (MCP `describe`) that `sprk_regardingorganization` + `sprk_regardingevent` lookups exist on `sprk_communication`. If `sprk_regardingevent` is absent, record it in notes and flag a schema follow-up (do NOT create schema here — outside this task's authorization).</step>
    <step order="4">Add the additive `sprk_event` entry to `RegardingLookupMap` (→ `sprk_regardingevent`), `RegardingFieldPriority`, and `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`.</step>
    <step order="5">Correct the org target: change the sender-domain match (and any other org-association write found in step 2) to resolve `sprk_organization` + write `sprk_regardingorganization`. Remove the `account` write path.</step>
    <step order="6">Add/update a unit test in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` asserting: (a) a sender-domain org match writes `sprk_regardingorganization` → `sprk_organization`, never `account`; (b) `sprk_event` resolves through the map (per NFR-08 test obligation).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (clean) + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication` (green).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB (incl. PDBs). Expected ≈ 0.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: run `/conflict-check` (BFF PR gate); invoke `code-review` on the diff; invoke `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus ADR-024 + org-target correctness). Address Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark task 004 ✅; confirm dependents 012/013 unblocked.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `current-task.md` per task-execute: status → completed; record the org-target correction + `sprk_event` wiring in Decisions Made.</step>
  </steps>

