  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Sender-domain org match writes `sprk_regardingorganization` → `sprk_organization`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep of `Services/Communication/` finds NO code path writing an OOB `account` (or OOB `organization`) regarding for org association.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`sprk_event` is present in `RegardingLookupMap`, `RegardingFieldPriority`, and `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A unit test asserts the corrected org target AND `sprk_event` resolution.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; existing + new Communication tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta reported (≈ 0 expected); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`/conflict-check` run before PR; Placement Justification in PR description.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    The org-target correction is a real behavioral bug fix, not cosmetic: the current code writes the wrong entity, so any org association resolved to `account` is downstream-invisible to Spaarke's `sprk_organization`-based views. Task 013 (W1) builds richer org-by-domain correlation on the corrected target.

    If `sprk_regardingevent` does not exist on `sprk_communication`, this task does NOT create it (schema creation is task 001's remit) — record the gap and flag a follow-up; the `sprk_event` catalog entries can still be wired, but note the runtime dependency on the column.

    Kept separate from task 003 because this touches inbound resolver domain-match LOGIC (behavioral, FULL) whereas 003 is purely additive.
  </notes>

